# Data layer & services

## Dependency injection — `Core/DI/DIContainer.swift`

`DIContainer` is a `Sendable` **struct** holding every service: `config`,
`authRepository`, `userRepository`, `profileRepository`,
`subscriptionRepository`, `purchasesService`, `analytics`,
`appleSignInService`, `cacheManager`. `DIContainer.makeDefault(config:)` is the
composition root — it picks `Supabase*` vs `Local*` per `config.backend`, wraps
profile/subscription repos in `Cached*` decorators when
`featureFlags.enableCaching`, and selects live-vs-noop analytics/purchases.

**Identical to the base kit — no Pro feature adds a container service**, and
none should. A container property referencing a Pro type would break compilation
the moment a buyer deleted that folder. Pro features use `@MainActor` `.shared`
singletons instead (`AppLockManager`, `LocalizationManager`, `ReviewManager`,
`GamificationEngine`, `ReminderScheduler`) — see `pro-features.mdc`.

Inject with `.inject(container)`; read with
`@Environment(\.container) private var container`. **Add a new core service** by
defining a protocol (+ a `Local`/`Noop` fallback), adding a stored property to
`DIContainer`, constructing it in `makeDefault`, and reading it from the
environment.

## Repository protocols (`Backend/Protocols/`)

| Protocol | Methods | Impls |
|---|---|---|
| `AuthRepository` | `signIn`, `signUp`→`SignUpOutcome`, `signInWithApple(idToken:nonce:)`, `signOut`, `currentUser` | `LocalAuthRepository` (actor) / `SupabaseAuthRepository` |
| `UserRepository` | `fetchCurrentUserProfile() -> User` | `LocalUserRepository` |
| `ProfileRepository` | `fetchProfile(for:)`, `upsertProfile(_:)`, `uploadAvatar(data:for:contentType:)` | `LocalProfileRepository` / `SupabaseProfileRepository` |
| `SubscriptionRepository` | `fetch(for:) -> SubscriptionStatus?` | `LocalSubscriptionRepository` (no Supabase impl) |

**Domain models** (all `Codable, Sendable`): `User{id,email}`,
`Profile{id,name,gender,contact,avatarURL,subscriptionStatus,updatedAt}`,
`Gender{unspecified,male,female,other}`, top-level
`SubscriptionStatus{plan,expiresAt}`, `SubscriptionPlan{free,pro,premium}`,
`SignUpOutcome{signedIn(User),confirmationEmailSent}`.

> Two distinct `SubscriptionStatus` types exist: the nested
> `Profile.SubscriptionStatus` (display-string enum) and the top-level struct
> used by `SubscriptionRepository`. Don't conflate them.

**Add a repository:** `protocol FooRepository: Sendable` + `LocalFooRepository`
in `Backend/Protocols/`; `SupabaseFooRepository` in `Backend/Supabase/` behind
`#if canImport(Supabase)`; wire selection into `makeDefault`; optionally add a
`Cached` decorator.

## Conditional SDK imports (keep the project SDK-optional)

```swift
#if canImport(RevenueCat)
purchases = RevenueCatPurchasesService(apiKey: Secrets.revenueCatAPIKey)
#else
purchases = NoopPurchasesService()   // demo data + warning log
#endif
```

Same for Supabase (→ `Local*`) and TelemetryDeck/TelemetryClient
(→ `NoopAnalyticsService`). Add a no-op/local branch for any new SDK.

## Caching (`Core/Cache/`)

Actor-based, two-tier (in-memory + dedicated `UserDefaults` suite).
`CacheManager.shared` conforms to `CacheStorage`: `get<T>(forKey:)`,
`set<T>(_:forKey:expiry:)`, `remove(forKey:)`, `removeAll()`,
`invalidate(matching:)` (wildcard `*`), `contains`, `allKeys`.

- Keys: extend the `CacheKeys` enum (e.g. `CacheKeys.profile(userId)`).
- Expiry: `CacheExpiry` `.never/.seconds/.minutes/.hours/.days`; named defaults
  in `CacheConfig`.
- Pattern: wrap a repo in a `Cached*` decorator **actor** — check cache, fall
  through to `remote`, write back; register behind `enableCaching`.
- Sign-out clears the cache via `CacheInvalidationObserver`.

## Services & app events

- `AnalyticsService`: `configure`, `track(_:properties:)`, `identify(userID:)`.
- `PurchasesService`: offerings/purchase/restore + `PurchaseOption` view model;
  `NoopPurchasesService` returns demo offerings.
- `AppleSignInServiceProtocol.authorize()` → `AppleSignInResult` (raw nonce +
  identity token) → `authRepository.signInWithApple(idToken:nonce:)`.
- `NotificationService.shared` (`@MainActor`): auth, local scheduling, APNs.
  **PRO** `ReminderScheduler.shared` builds on top of it.
- `AppLogger.log(_:level:)` (DEBUG-only) instead of bare `print`.
- **App events** (`Core/Utils/AppEvents.swift`): `.authStatusDidChange`,
  `.profileDidChange`, `.subscriptionDidChange`, `.userDidSignOut` (payload keys
  via `SubscriptionEventKey`). Post on state change; observe with
  `.onReceive(NotificationCenter…)`.

Tests use **XCTest** with `@testable import TheSwiftKit` (`Tests/`); keep them
offline via the `.local` backend / `Local*` repos.
